      "content": "That's a great start, really clean. \n\nOne thing though—the automated system flagged this draft because the Completeness Score is extremely low. It's basically hitting the floor. I know I said not to pad it, but the documentation team is worried that if it's too brief, engineers will skip over it or feel like they're missing context.\n\nCan you expand on this a bit? Try to add more technical depth or context around the steps (like explaining *why* we need the prerequisites or what the commands are actually doing in the background) to get that score up a little higher. Just please make sure it still feels professional and doesn't just become a wall of nonsense text.",
